/P 166 0 R
/T (1.2 Importance of the Problem)
/E (1.2 Importance of the Problem)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (The gap between how a robot behaves under a traditional OS and how it behaves under an RTOS is not theoretical. In the real world, that gap translates into missed deadlines, inconsistent movements, and safety failures. A robotic arm that cannot guarantee its 100-millisecond motion update will arrive exactly on time is an arm whose position at any moment cannot be fully trusted.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
