585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (This work examines how a five-jointed robotic arm moves through space. Using MATLAB, the team ran simulations before any physical construction began. Rather than assemble hardware right away, they focused on equations that describe motion. To map position changes, both forward and reverse calculations guided the analysis. Problems often show up sooner when virtual testing comes first. Early detection becomes possible by working inside simulated environments. This paper validates the model-in-the-loop approach used here, where simulation precedes physical deployment.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
