<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Starting with motion capture, Mankani's group built a mechanical limb capable of saving sequences. Once taught, it replays actions without human input. Repetitive factory jobs benefit from this behavior loop. Wireless internet access forms part of the setup. Remote operation becomes possible due to network connectivity. The teach-and-replay system described directly inspired the sequence recording and transmission feature of M.A.T.R.I.X., where the operator manually poses the arm and sends the recorded sequence to QNX for RTOS-controlled replay.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
