/T (This image shows the QNX Momentics IDE with the MATRIX_Robotic_ARM.c file open and the program running live on the QNX 8.0 virtual machine. The console panel at the bottom shows that the Motion Task launched at priority 10 with a 100 ms period, the Safety Task launched at priority 20 as the HIGHEST priority thread, and the system came online with instructions to use the dashboard, select RTOS mode, record poses, and send them to QNX. The source code visible in the editor shows the thread launch section using launch_rt_thread with PRIO_SAFETY and PRIO_MOTION constants. This confirms that the POSIX real-time threads are launching correctly under SCHED_FIFO scheduling on QNX and that the TCP connection to the bridge is established)
