/P 185 0 R
/T (This image shows the QNX console during a complete sequence execution. The RECV thread received a SEQ_START command for 6 poses with 1000 ms duration each, followed by all six POSE entries containing the exact joint angle values recorded on the dashboard. After SEQ_END was received, the Motion Task executed each pose in order, printing POSE_DONE after each one and ending with SEQ_COMPLETE. The joint angle values visible in the log, such as Pose 3 with values 70.5, 82.5, 84.0, 86.5, 103.5, and 62.0, match exactly what was captured on the dashboard. This confirms that the full teach-to-replay pipeline works correctly and that QNX is executing the recorded sequence under RTOS control with deterministic 1000 ms timing per pose.)
/E (This image shows the QNX console during a complete sequence execution. The RECV thread received a SEQ_START command for 6 poses with 1000 ms duration each, followed by all six POSE entries containing the exact joint angle values recorded on the dashboard. After SEQ_END was received, the Motion Task executed each pose in order, printing POSE_DONE after each one and ending with SEQ_COMPLETE. The joint angle values visible in the log, such as Pose 3 with values 70.5, 82.5, 84.0, 86.5, 103.5, and 62.0, match exactly what was captured on the dashboard. This confirms that the full teach-to-replay pipeline works correctly and that QNX is executing the recorded sequence under RTOS control with deterministic 1000 ms timing per pose.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
789 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 185 0 R
/T (This image shows the most critical result of the project: the emergency stop being triggered while the system is running in RTOS mode. The entire dashboard has switched to a red overlay with the EMERGENCY STOP warning displayed prominently in the centre. The arm model has turned red and frozen in its current position, and the event log on the right confirms the sequence of events with timestamps showing EMERGENCY STOP from QNX Safety Task preempted at 23:14:51. The operating mode panel on the left shows RTOS selected and the status bar at the bottom shows the arm was mid-sequence at Pose 1 of 4 when the stop was triggered. This confirms thatjf the Safety Task at priority 25 successfully preempted the Motion Task and that the stop reached the browser within a single network round-trip, which is the core result this project was built to demonstrate.)
/E (This image shows the most critical result of the project: the emergency stop being triggered while the system is running in RTOS mode. The entire dashboard has switched to a red overlay with the EMERGENCY STOP warning displayed prominently in the centre. The arm model has turned red and frozen in its current position, and the event log on the right confirms the sequence of events with timestamps showing EMERGENCY STOP from QNX Safety Task preempted at 23:14:51. The operating mode panel on the left shows RTOS selected and the status bar at the bottom shows the arm was mid-sequence at Pose 1 of 4 when the stop was triggered. This confirms thatjf the Safety Task at priority 25 successfully preempted the Motion Task and that the stop reached the browser within a single network round-trip, which is the core result this project was built to demonstrate.)
