/T (This image shows one of the most important results: the QNX Safety Task intercepting an emergency stop command in the middle of a running sequence. The console shows that a 5-pose sequence had started and was executing normally, with Pose 0 done and Pose 1 just beginning, when the RECV thread received EMERGENCY_STOP from the bridge. The Motion Task immediately printed EMERGENCY MID-POSE 1, STOPPING NOW, followed by Sequence aborted and Emergency halted. This confirms that the Safety Task at the highest priority correctly interrupted the Motion Task mid-execution without waiting for the current pose to complete, which is exactly the preemptive RTOS behaviour this project was designed to demonstrate and validate)
/E (This image shows one of the most important results: the QNX Safety Task intercepting an emergency stop command in the middle of a running sequence. The console shows that a 5-pose sequence had started and was executing normally, with Pose 0 done and Pose 1 just beginning, when the RECV thread received EMERGENCY_STOP from the bridge. The Motion Task immediately printed EMERGENCY MID-POSE 1, STOPPING NOW, followed by Sequence aborted and Emergency halted. This confirms that the Safety Task at the highest priority correctly interrupted the Motion Task mid-execution without waiting for the current pose to complete, which is exactly the preemptive RTOS behaviour this project was designed to demonstrate and validate)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
