802 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (Across all fifteen figures, the system demonstrated consistent and correct behaviour in every tested scenario. The model upload and axis calibration pipeline worked cleanly for ten STL components. The dashboard rendered the assembled arm in real time at 60 FPS with correct joint hierarchy and gripper animation. The Python bridge successfully relayed data in both directions across TCP and WebSocket without any packet loss. The QNX RTOS controller launched all threads at their correct priorities, executed full pose sequences with deterministic 1000 ms timing, and responded to emergency stop commands mid-execution through immediate Safety Task preemption. The NON-RTOS mode correctly simulated sequential joint movement and delayed emergency response, providing a clear visual contrast against RTOS behaviour. Taken together, these results confirm that the M.A.T.R.I.X. system works as designed from end to end)
/E (Across all fifteen figures, the system demonstrated consistent and correct behaviour in every tested scenario. The model upload and axis calibration pipeline worked cleanly for ten STL components. The dashboard rendered the assembled arm in real time at 60 FPS with correct joint hierarchy and gripper animation. The Python bridge successfully relayed data in both directions across TCP and WebSocket without any packet loss. The QNX RTOS controller launched all threads at their correct priorities, executed full pose sequences with deterministic 1000 ms timing, and responded to emergency stop commands mid-execution through immediate Safety Task preemption. The NON-RTOS mode correctly simulated sequential joint movement and delayed emergency response, providing a clear visual contrast against RTOS behaviour. Taken together, these results confirm that the M.A.T.R.I.X. system works as designed from end to end)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
