812 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 188 0 R
/E ( RTOS vs NON-RTOS In RTOS mode, joint updates at the browser stayed within about plus or minus 2 to 3 milliseconds of the 100 ms target, even in long runs. The arm looked perfectly smooth throughout. In NON-RTOS mode under simulated load, those same intervals jumped around between 20 and 80 milliseconds. That is what produced the choppy, uneven arm motion that made the comparison so easy to see.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
