1897 0 obj
<<
/Title (Robotic systems require precise timing, coordinated motion, and reliable safety mechanisms to ensure stable operation. In many conventional embedded implementations, motion control is handled using sequential programming structures, where task execution depends on loop timing and processor load. This approach often leads to unpredictable behavior when system complexity increases.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1706 0 R
/Next 1898 0 R
>>
endobj
1898 0 obj
<<
/Title (Real-Time Operating Systems \(RTOS\) address this challenge by providing deterministic scheduling, task prioritization, and guaranteed execution intervals for critical operations. In robotic control systems, RTOS ensures that motion commands, safety monitoring, and communication processes operate predictably even under varying computational loads.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1706 0 R
/Prev 1897 0 R
>>
endobj
