/Title (This image shows the most critical result of the project: the emergency stop being triggered while the system is running in RTOS mode. The entire dashboard has switched to a red overlay with the EMERGENCY STOP warning displayed prominently in the centre. The arm model has turned red and frozen in its current position, and the event log on the right confirms the sequence of events with timestamps showing EMERGENCY STOP from QNX Safety Task preempted at 23:14:51. The operating mode panel on the left shows RTOS selected and the status bar at the bottom shows the arm was mid-sequence at Pose 1 of 4 when the stop was triggered. This confirms that the Safety Task at priority 25 successfully preempted the Motion Task and that the stop reached the browser within a single network round-trip, which is the core result this project was built to demonstrate.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2248 0 R
/Next 2244 0 R
>>
endobj
2247 0 obj
<<
/Title (This image shows the axis calibration screen, which is Step 2 of the setup flow. The user selects each uploaded model from the list on the left and clicks four points around the circular rim of its hinge joint on the 3D view. The system then calculates the geometric center automatically and marks it with a crosshair. It can be observed that Base.STL and Gripper base.STL are already marked as SET with green ticks, while the remaining parts are waiting to be calibrated. The green point markers and the crosshair lines are clearly visible on the base component in the 3D view. This step ensures that each joint rotates around its correct physical axis when the arm is animated)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
